# a callee whose loop leaves by a `return` under a `try` is copied, and a guess at a value from in front of that loop would have the loop built twice. Each return of the copy leads on behind the call
# the block of the return throws to the handler, which goes on with the loop: so it is a member of the loop. It was "the walk is over and an edge leads to a block that has no end"
# f2 = deed
# -- source: callee-copied-with-a-loop-that-returns-under-a-handler-comes-to-its-end.ts
